  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "script-without-config",
      "lines": [
        "composer.json script test:integration runs phpunit with phpunit.integration.xml, which is not in the checkout.",
        "  phpunit -c phpunit.integration.xml --fail-on-warning",
        "  The command is there to be run, so whoever runs it gets a tool that has nothing to go by - and CI, if it runs the script, reports the failure as the change under test."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL-3.0-or-later (appinfo/info.xml), agpl (package.json), LICENSES/ holds AGPL-3.0-or-later.txt, Apache-2.0.txt, CC-BY-4.0.txt, CC0-1.0.txt, LicenseRef-DiasporaTrademarks.txt, LicenseRef-FacebookTrademarks.txt, LicenseRef-InstagramTrademarks.txt, LicenseRef-MastodonTrademarks.txt, LicenseRef-TumblrTrademarks.txt, MIT.txt.",
        "  No SPDX id: agpl (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support",
      "lines": [
        "PHP floors differ: appinfo/info.xml says min-version 8.2, composer.json requires php >=8.1 <=8.4.",
        "  The info.xml floor is the one that applies: the server does not enable the app below it. The composer requirement can be raised to 8.2."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "php-support-max",
      "lines": [
        "appinfo/info.xml caps PHP at max-version 8.5.",
        "  A server on a newer PHP refuses to enable the app, so this cap has to be raised deliberately with every PHP release, not left where it was."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^24.0.0 (package.json engines.node).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The workflows read node-version from a variable, which is not resolved here, so whether CI builds on that major is not decidable from the checkout."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.mjs), Stylelint (stylelint.config.cjs), Psalm (psalm.xml), PHPUnit (phpunit.xml), PHP-CS-Fixer (.php-cs-fixer.dist.php), REUSE (REUSE.toml).",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "1 declared package is named nowhere in the checkout: ts-loader.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 456 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
